---
layout: layouts/tool.njk
toolSlug: salary-to-hourly-calculator
title: "Salary to Hourly Calculator (and Hourly to Salary)"
description: "Convert pay between annual, monthly, bi-weekly, weekly, daily and hourly rates using your hours per week, paid weeks per year and unpaid time off."
permalink: /tools/salary-to-hourly-calculator/
h1: "Salary to Hourly Calculator"
extraCss: "/tools/salary-to-hourly-calculator/style.css"
quickAnswer: "Hourly rate = annual salary ÷ (hours per week × paid weeks per year). At 40 hours and 52 weeks that is 2,080 hours, so 52,000 a year is 25.00 an hour. Going the other way, 30 an hour is 62,400 a year and 5,200 a month. Two unpaid weeks off leaves 50 paid weeks, which raises the hourly equivalent of 52,000 to 26.00."
formula:
  title: "Pay Conversion Formula"
  expression: "Hourly = Annual ÷ (Hours per week × Paid weeks)   ·   Annual = Hourly × Hours per week × Paid weeks   ·   Monthly = Annual ÷ 12"
  explanation: "Every input is first turned into an annual figure, then divided out. Paid weeks are the weeks in the year minus any unpaid weeks off. Weekly pay is annual ÷ paid weeks, bi-weekly is two of those weeks, daily is weekly ÷ days worked per week, and hourly is weekly ÷ hours per week. Monthly pay is always annual ÷ 12, because months are not a whole number of weeks."
  variables:
    - name: "Hours per week"
      description: "Your contracted or usual paid hours, such as 40 or 37.5."
    - name: "Paid weeks per year"
      description: "52 for most salaried jobs (paid holidays count as paid weeks)."
    - name: "Unpaid weeks off"
      description: "Weeks you are not paid for, such as unpaid leave or gaps between contracts."
workedExamples:
  - title: "52,000 a year to hourly"
    inputs:
      - "Pay: 52,000 per year"
      - "40 hours per week, 52 paid weeks"
    steps:
      - "Hours per year: 40 × 52 = 2,080"
      - "Hourly: 52,000 ÷ 2,080 = 25.00"
    result: "25.00 per hour (1,000 per week, 4,333.33 per month)"
    link: "/tools/salary-to-hourly-calculator/?amount=52000&per=annual&hours=40&weeks=52#tool"
  - title: "30 an hour to yearly and monthly"
    inputs:
      - "Pay: 30 per hour"
      - "40 hours per week, 52 paid weeks"
    steps:
      - "Annual: 30 × 40 × 52 = 62,400"
      - "Monthly: 62,400 ÷ 12 = 5,200"
    result: "62,400 per year, 5,200 per month"
    link: "/tools/salary-to-hourly-calculator/?amount=30&per=hourly&hours=40&weeks=52#tool"
  - title: "52,000 a year with two unpaid weeks"
    inputs:
      - "Pay: 52,000 per year"
      - "40 hours per week, 52 weeks, 2 unpaid weeks off"
    steps:
      - "Paid weeks: 52 − 2 = 50"
      - "Hours worked: 40 × 50 = 2,000"
      - "Hourly: 52,000 ÷ 2,000 = 26.00"
    result: "26.00 per hour for the hours actually worked"
    link: "/tools/salary-to-hourly-calculator/?amount=52000&per=annual&hours=40&weeks=52&unpaid=2#tool"
commonMistakes:
  - title: "Multiplying weekly pay by 4 to get monthly pay"
    description: "A year has 52 weeks but only 48 if you count four per month. Monthly pay is annual ÷ 12, which is weekly pay × 4.33. Using × 4 understates monthly income by about 8%."
  - title: "Comparing a salary with an hourly rate without counting holidays"
    description: "A salaried job usually pays for holidays and sick days; a contractor's hourly rate often does not. To compare fairly, enter the contractor's unpaid weeks off so the annual figure reflects the weeks they will actually bill."
  - title: "Treating bi-weekly as semi-monthly"
    description: "Bi-weekly means every two weeks, which is 26 paychecks a year. Semi-monthly means twice a month, which is 24. On the same salary a bi-weekly paycheck is smaller than a semi-monthly one."
  - title: "Using gross figures as take-home pay"
    description: "These are gross amounts before income tax, social security, pension and other deductions. Use a salary tax calculator for take-home pay."
  - title: "Ignoring overtime and unpaid extra hours"
    description: "If you regularly work more than your contracted hours without extra pay, your real hourly rate is lower. Enter the hours you actually work to see it."
faqs:
  - q: "How do I convert my salary to an hourly rate?"
    a: "Divide your annual salary by the number of hours you are paid for in a year. At 40 hours a week for 52 weeks that is 2,080 hours, so divide the salary by 2,080."
  - q: "How much is 52,000 a year per hour?"
    a: "52,000 a year is 25.00 an hour at 40 hours a week for 52 weeks. At 37.5 hours a week it is 26.67 an hour."
  - q: "How much is 30 an hour annually?"
    a: "30 an hour is 62,400 a year at 40 hours a week and 52 paid weeks, which is 5,200 a month and 1,200 a week."
  - q: "How many working hours are in a year?"
    a: "A 40-hour week for 52 weeks is 2,080 hours. A year is actually 52 weeks and 1 or 2 days, so some employers use 2,087 hours; the US Office of Personnel Management uses 2,087 for federal hourly rates."
  - q: "How do I calculate monthly salary from hourly pay?"
    a: "Multiply the hourly rate by hours per week and by 52 to get annual pay, then divide by 12. For 20 an hour at 40 hours: 20 × 40 × 52 ÷ 12 = 3,466.67 a month."
  - q: "What is the difference between bi-weekly and semi-monthly pay?"
    a: "Bi-weekly pay comes every two weeks, 26 times a year. Semi-monthly pay comes twice a month, 24 times a year. The calculator shows the bi-weekly amount."
  - q: "Does this include tax?"
    a: "No. All figures are gross pay before tax and deductions. The ToolsBuilt salary tax calculators show take-home pay for several countries."
sources:
  - name: "U.S. Office of Personnel Management: Computing hourly rates of pay using the 2,087-hour divisor"
    url: "https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/pay-leave/pay-administration/fact-sheets/computing-hourly-rates-of-pay-using-the-2087-hour-divisor/"
  - name: "U.S. Department of Labor: Overtime pay (FLSA)"
    url: "https://www.dol.gov/agencies/whd/overtime"
  - name: "GOV.UK: National Minimum Wage and National Living Wage rates"
    url: "https://www.gov.uk/national-minimum-wage-rates"
lastReviewed: "2026-10-31"
howto:
  name: "How to Convert Salary to Hourly Pay"
  description: "Convert any pay rate into annual, monthly, bi-weekly, weekly, daily and hourly figures."
  steps:
    - name: "Enter your pay"
      text: "Type the amount and choose whether it is per hour, day, week, two weeks, month or year."
    - name: "Set your working pattern"
      text: "Enter hours per week, days per week and paid weeks per year (40, 5 and 52 by default)."
    - name: "Add unpaid time off"
      text: "Enter any unpaid weeks off, such as unpaid leave or gaps between contracts."
    - name: "Read every pay period"
      text: "See the same pay as an annual, monthly, bi-weekly, weekly, daily and hourly amount."
---
{% from "partials/currency-select.njk" import currencySelect, countryData with context %}
{{ countryData(countries) }}

    <!-- Tool Form Container -->
    <section class="tool-container" aria-label="Salary to Hourly Calculator">
      <form id="calculator-form" novalidate>
        <div class="form-grid salary-pay-grid">
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="amount">Pay <span class="text-accent">*</span></label>
            <input type="number" inputmode="decimal" step="any" min="0" id="amount" data-param="amount" class="form-control" value="52000" required aria-required="true">
          </div>
          <div class="form-group">
            <label for="period">Paid</label>
            <select id="period" data-param="per" class="form-control">
              <option value="hourly">per hour</option>
              <option value="daily">per day</option>
              <option value="weekly">per week</option>
              <option value="biweekly">every two weeks</option>
              <option value="monthly">per month</option>
              <option value="annual" selected>per year</option>
            </select>
          </div>
          {{ currencySelect({ id: "currency", param: "cur", selected: "USD" }) }}
        </div>

        <fieldset class="salary-fieldset">
          <legend>Working pattern</legend>
          <div class="form-grid salary-pattern-grid">
            <div class="form-group">
              <label for="hours">Hours per week</label>
              <input type="number" inputmode="decimal" step="any" min="0" max="168" id="hours" data-param="hours" class="form-control" value="40">
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
              <label for="days">Days per week</label>
              <input type="number" inputmode="decimal" step="any" min="0" max="7" id="days" data-param="days" class="form-control" value="5">
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
              <label for="weeks">Weeks per year</label>
              <input type="number" inputmode="decimal" step="any" min="1" max="53" id="weeks" data-param="weeks" class="form-control" value="52">
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
              <label for="unpaid">Unpaid weeks off</label>
              <input type="number" inputmode="decimal" step="any" min="0" id="unpaid" data-param="unpaid" class="form-control" value="0">
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="form-hint">Paid holidays count as paid weeks. Only enter weeks you are not paid for as unpaid weeks off.</p>
        </fieldset>

        <div class="button-group mt-6">
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Convert Pay</button>
          <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" id="reset-btn">Reset</button>
        </div>
      </form>

      <div id="error-box" class="hidden form-error" role="alert"></div>

      <div id="result-box" class="result-box is-visible" aria-live="polite">
